<title>UK: AHB adds 500 million marks to Jan 2003 bond.</title>
<headline>AHB adds 500 million marks to Jan 2003 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 2.0 billion marks from 1.5 billion marks, joint lead managers Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, DG Bank and Dresdner Kleinwort Benson said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ALLGEMEINE HYPOTHEKENBANK</p>
<p> AMT   *2.0 BLN	 COUPON     5.00	MATURITY    23.JAN.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE ***23.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+4 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    FFURT     PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.125 PCT JAN 2003 TREUHAND</p>
<p> NOTES	**TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>		 *ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 1.0 BLN MARKS ON 13.JAN.97</p>
<p>	     ***PLUS ACCRUED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
